      "content": "I see. But what if the physician actually uses terms that are even more specific about the strange appearance? For example, if they mention things like \"rugged, cave-like skin textures\" or \"pronounced, pointed protrusions\" that don't match any known dermatological condition? Is there a specific way to categorize these morphological anomalies in the L-series so they don't just look like we're making up symptoms?",
